  {
    "name": "a5_geometry_to_cells",
    "categories": ["Geometry Integration"],
    "relatedFunctions": ["a5_cell_to_geometry", "a5_uncompact", "a5_contains"],
    "description": "Returns the A5 cells covering an arbitrary geometry at the given resolution. Points map to their containing cell, lines are traced, and polygons are filled by cell-center containment by default (holes excluded); MULTI* and GEOMETRYCOLLECTION inputs are unioned. The optional third `overlapping` argument additionally includes cells that merely touch the polygon boundary, for genuinely gap-free coverage. A geometry with polygon parts comes back as a **covering** — compacted cells in curve order followed by a compaction marker that is not a cell — which is the right shape for storage and set operations; point- and line-only geometries return their plain cells. Call `a5_uncompact` before unnesting or drawing a covering: it drops the marker and expands every cell to the resolution the covering was built at (cell boundaries at different resolutions don't nest geometrically, so drawing a compacted result shows phantom gaps)."
  }
]
